            A
            %strong moduli stack of elliptic curves
            is, as the name suggests, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            which classifies
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            such that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            any other suitable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            between them is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalent
            to that of
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
            with equivalences between these. (There are some variants of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            corresponding to the choice of which singularities and degeneracies of elliptic curves are taken into account.)
          %p
            This is formalized in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            here is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            in general. The moduli stack always has a tautological construction as a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
            to the groupoid of suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represented
            by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+stack"} geometric stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} dually
            given by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebroid"} Hopf algebroid
          %p
            The moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+compactification"} compactification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mover
                      %mi ell
                      %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{\overline{ell}}
            obtained by adding the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+cubic+curve"} nodal cubic curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cuspidal+cubic+curve"} cuspidal cubic curve
            and hence all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubic+curves"} cubic curves
            produces the full moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi cub
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{cub}
            of cubic curves, inside which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            sits as the locus of non-singular curves.
          %p
            Since an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+genus"} genus-1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curve"} algebraic curve
            with a marked point (the neutral element of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            structure),
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+algebraic+curves"} moduli stack of algebraic curves
            for genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 1
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            punctures, and as such is often equivalently written
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{M}_{1,1} = \mathcal{M}_{ell}
                  \\,.
          %p
            A special class of cases which is much simpler than the general case but still of paramount interest is the moduli stack of elliptic curves over the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi ell
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{C}) \to \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tori"} tori
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surfaces"} Riemann surfaces
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
            1 which may be identified with quotients of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            by a framed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            well-defined up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%C3%B6bius+transformations"} Möbius transformations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            quotient) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half+plane"} upper half plane
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+curves"} moduli space of curves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{(1,1)}
            which in turn is a quotient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teichm%C3%BCller+space"} Teichmüller space
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_{(1,1)}
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#DescriptionOverTheComplexNumbers"} Description over the complex numbers
              \.
          %p Below that is the
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#DescriptionOverGeneralSchemes"} Description over general schemes
              \.
          %p
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stack"} algebraic stack
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi ell
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goerss-Hopkins-Miller+theorem"} Goerss-Hopkins-Miller theorem
            the assignment to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+spectrum"} elliptic spectrum
            lifts the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            to a higher structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            in a way that makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{M}_{ell}, \mathcal{O}^{op})
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Deligne-Mumford+stack"} spectral Deligne-Mumford stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+sections"} global sections
            of this structure sheaf yield the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} topological modular forms
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#InEInfinityGeometry"} As a derived scheme in E-infinity geometry
          %p
            See also
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology+-+elliptic+curves"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology - elliptic curves
            for more.
          %h2#DescriptionOverTheComplexNumbers Description over the complex numbers
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to Spec(\mathbb{C})
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            is determined, up to non-canonical
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j(E) \in \mathbb{C}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex number
            appears as a value, and therefore the moduli space of elliptic cuves a priori is not
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactification"} compactification
            of the moduli space is obtained by including also elliptic curves with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+singularity"} nodal singularity
          %h3#upper_half_plane Upper half plane
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half+plane"} upper half plane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{h}
            is in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            with framed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattices"} lattices
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            classes of framed elliptic curves over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi framed
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi lattices
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi in
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi framed
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi elliptic
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi curves
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi over
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathfrak{h}
                  \\simeq
                  \\{framed\;lattices\;in\;\mathbb{C}\}
                  \\simeq
                  \\{framed\;elliptic\;curves\;over\;\mathbb{C}\}/_\sim
          %p and we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi elliptic
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi curves
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi over
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∼
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{elliptic\;curves\;over\;\mathbb{C}\}_\sim
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathfrak{h}/{SL_2(\mathbb{Z})}
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+linear+group"} special linear group
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi SL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi a
                            %mtd
                              %mi b
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi c
                            %mtd
                              %mi d
                      %mo )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi a
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mi c
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SL_2(\mathbb{Z}) = \left\{ \left(\array{a &amp; b \\ c &amp; d }\right)| a d - c d = 1\right\}
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acts
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%C3%B6bius+transformations"} Möbius transformations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ↦
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi τ
                      %mo +
                      %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mi τ
                      %mo +
                      %mi d
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau \mapsto \frac{a \tau + b}{c \tau + d}
                  \\,.
          %h3#the_naive_moduli_space_and_its_problems The naive moduli space and its problems
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi 𝔥
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    M_{1,1} := \mathfrak{h}/SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            %p
              for the plain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half+plane"} upper half plane
              by the above group action.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                holomorphic family of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : X \to T
              %li
                %p
                  together with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo :
                        %mi T
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : T \to X
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                  such that for any
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in T
                  the pair
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi t
                        %mo ,
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_t, s(t))
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
                  (using the first definition above).
          %p For every family
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi π
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X \\ \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\pi}} \\ T
                  }
          %p
            we would like to have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to M_{1,1}
            such that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo *
                          %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi ϕ
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X \simeq \phi^* F &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; F
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  T &amp;\stackrel{\phi}{\longrightarrow}&amp; M_{1,1}
                  }
          %p where
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi:   t \mapsto [X_t, s(t)]
          %p such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : T \to M_{1,1}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+map"} holomorphic map
            %li
              %p
                every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+map"} holomorphic map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \to M_{1,1}
                corresponds to a family over
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              %p
                there is a universal family over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{1,1}
          %p
            This is
            %em impossible
            \. One can construct explicit counterexamples. These counterexamples involve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
            with nontrivial
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
          %p For instance
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo −
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{
                  (x,y,z) \in \mathbb{P}^2 \times X :
                  y^2 = x(x-1)(x-\lambda)
                  \\}
                  \\to
                  X := \mathbb{P}^1 - \{0,1,\infty\}
          %blockquote
            %p
              but see the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
              for a discussion of the statement “it’s the automorphisms that prevent the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
              from existing”
          %h3#moduli_space_of_framed_elliptic_curves Moduli space of framed elliptic curves
          %p consider
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi 𝔥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{Z}^2 \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C} \times \mathfrak{h}
          %p given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo +
                  %mi m
                  %mi τ
                  %mo +
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (m,n) :
                  (z,\tau)
                  \\mapsto
                  (z + m \tau + n, \tau)
          %p Then consider the family
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %mo :
                          %mo =
                          %mi ℂ
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mn 2
                          %mo ×
                          %mi 𝔥
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝔥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  E := \mathbb{C}/_{\mathbb{Z}^2} \times \mathfrak{h}
                  \\\ \downarrow \\ \mathfrak{h}
                  }
          %p
            is a family of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{h}
          %p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi τ
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\tau = \mathbb{C}/{\Lambda_\tau}
            with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi τ
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Lambda_{\tau} := \mathbb{Z}\cdot 1 \oplus \mathbb{Z}\cdot \tau
          %p is a family of framed elliptic curves.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{h}
              with the family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝔥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to \mathfrak{h}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fine+moduli+space"} fine moduli space
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+elliptic+curves"} framed elliptic curves
          %p
            Consider any map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : T \to \mathfrak{h}
          %p with pullback of the universal family
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ?
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo *
                          %mi E
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ϕ
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝔥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X \stackrel{?}{\to} \phi^* E &amp;\to &amp; E
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  T &amp;\stackrel{\phi}{\to}&amp;
                  \\mathfrak{h}
                  }
          %p
            %strong claim
            for every point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in T
            there is an open neighbourhood
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_0 \in U \hookrightarrow T
            such that one can choose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} 1-forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_t
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\tau
            which vary holomorphically with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
          %p
            Notice that
            %em locally
            every family of elliptic curves is framed (since we can locally extend a choice of basis for
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝔥
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi SL
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi Id
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathfrak{h}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{SL_2(\mathbb{Z})}
                  \\\
                  M_{1,1} &amp;\stackrel{Id}{\to}&amp;
                  M_{1,1}
                  }
          %p
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi π
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho = e^{2\pi i/6}
            ,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo ±
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = \{\pm I\}
          %p
            isn’t locally liftable at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            so it is not a univresal family of unframed curves.
          %h3#moduli_stackorbifold_of_elliptic_curves Moduli stack/orbifold of elliptic curves
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Consider the global
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+stack"} quotient stack
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi 𝔥
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{M}_{1,1} := \mathfrak{h}//SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            %p
              of the upper half plane by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+linear+group"} special linear group
              over the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of elliptic curves.
          %h3#compactified_moduli_stack Compactified moduli stack
          %p
            Consider the complex analytic parameterization over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/annulus"} annulus
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi q
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{q \in \mathbb{C} | 0 \lt {\vert q \vert} \lt 1 \}
          %p of elliptic curves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi q
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_q \coloneqq \mathbb{C}^*/q^{\mathbb{Z}}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This has an extension to the origin, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_0
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+neighbourhood"} formal neighbourhood
            of the origin, hence over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{Z}[ [q] ])
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+curve"} Tate curve
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, section 4.3
            ).
          %h2#DescriptionOverGeneralSchemes Description over general schemes
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubic+curve"} cubic curve
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon X \to S
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \colon S \to X
            and such that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski locally
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is given by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}_S^2
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 4
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  y^2 + a_1 x y = x^3 + a_2 x^2 + a_4 x + a_6
          %p
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \colon S \to X
            is the line at infinity.
          %p
            Equivalently this says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+morphism"} proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+morphism"} flat morphism
            with a section contained in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+locus"} smooth locus
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            are geometrically integral curves of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+genus"} arithmetic genus
            one.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi cub
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{cub}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of such
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubic+curves"} cubic curves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi cub
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 12
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \in H^0(\mathcal{M}_{cub}, \omega^{12})
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi cub
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi FG
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{M}_{ell} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{M}_{cub}
                  \\longrightarrow \mathcal{M}_{FG}.
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            for details. (A textbook account is in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Silverman09"} Silverman 09, III
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            is in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Mathew"} Mathew, section 3
          %p
            Two standard versions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebroids"} Hopf algebroids
            representing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mover
                      %mi ell
                      %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{\overline{ell}}
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+stack"} geometric stack
            are usefully reviewed in (
            %a{:href => "#Mathew"}> Mathew, section 4
            ).
          %h2#InEInfinityGeometry
            As a derived scheme in
            = succeed "-geometry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goerss-Hopkins-Miller+theorem"} Goerss-Hopkins-Miller theorem
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            of the moduli stack of elliptic curves lifts to a sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{top}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            which over a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            is the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+spectrum"} elliptic spectrum
          %p
            By (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"}> Lurie (Survey), theorem 4.1
            ), this yields a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Deligne-Mumford+stack"} spectral Deligne-Mumford stack
            refinement
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                    %mi der
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{M}_{ell}^{der} \coloneqq  (\mathcal{M}_{ell}, \mathcal{O}^{top})
          %p
            which is the moduli stack of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+elliptic+curves"} derived elliptic curves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalence"} natural equivalence
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                    %mi der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom(Spec(A), \mathcal{M}_{ell}^{der})
                  \\simeq
                  E(A)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the left we have maps of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} structured (∞,1)-toposes
            and on the right the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+elliptic+curves"} derived elliptic curves
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            This is based on the representability theorem (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"}> Lurie (Survey), prop. 4.1
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Representability+Theorems"} Lurie (Representability)
          %p
            In this derived picture the compactified dericed moduli space is obtained by gluing in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+K-theory"} Tate K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi KU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KO[ [q] ] \simeq KU[ [q] ]/\mathbb{Z}_2
            by forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ℳ
                            %mi ell
                            %mi der
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spec
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ℳ
                            %mover
                              %mi ell
                              %mo ¯
                            %mi der
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Spec(K((q))) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \mathcal{M}_{ell}^{der}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  Spec(K[ [q] ]) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \mathcal{M}_{\overline{ell}}^{der}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"}> Lurie(Survey), p. 33
            ). Again, the underlying ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+stack"} Deligne-Mumford stack
            is the ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mover
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{\overline{\ell}}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#finite_covers Finite covers
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}[n]
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves+with+level-n+structure"} elliptic curves with level-n structure
            (for some
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            (similarly for the compactifications).
          %p
            (Over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            this is the
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+curve"} modular curve
          %h3#cohomology Cohomology
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 12
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_1(\mathcal{M}_{1,1}, \mathbb{Z})
                    \= \mathbb{Z}/12\mathbb{Z}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^1(\mathcal{M}_{1,1}, \mathbb{Z}) = 0
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 12
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^2(\mathcal{M}_{1,1}, \mathbb{Z})
                    \= \mathbb{Z}/12 \mathbb{Z}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_\bullet(\mathcal{M}_{1,1}, \mathbb{Q})
                    \\simeq
                    H_\bullet(M_{1,1}, \mathbb{Q})
            %p
              and similarly for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 12
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(\mathcal{M}_{1,1}) = -\frac{1}{12}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Pic
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 12
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Pic(\mathcal{M}_{1,1}) \simeq \mathbb{Z}/12\mathbb{Z}
          %h3#EulerCharacteristic Euler characteristic
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+Euler+characteristic"} orbifold Euler characteristic
            of the moduli space of complex elliptic curves is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+values+of+L-functions"} special value
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+zeta+function"} Riemann zeta function
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s= -1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ζ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 12
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi(\mathcal{M}_{1,1}) = \zeta(-1) = - \frac{1}{12}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is a special case of the result in (
            %a{:href => "#ZagierHarer86"}> Zagier-Harer 86
            ) discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+curves"} moduli space of curves
