          %h2#references References
          %p
            Introductory lecture notes on the moduli space of elliptic curves over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            include
          %ul
            %li#Hain08
              %p
                Richard Hain,
                %em Lectures on Moduli Spaces of Elliptic Curves
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.1803"}> arXiv:0812.1803
                )
            %li#IntroOrbifolds
              %p
                section 4 of
                %em Introduction to Orbifolds
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/IntroductionToOrbifolds.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p Accounts of the general case include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Nicholas M. Katz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barry+Mazur"} Barry Mazur
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Arithmetic moduli of elliptic curves
            %li#Silverman09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Silverman"}> Joseph Silverman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The arithmetic of elliptic curves
          %p Lecture notes/talk notes reviewing this include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                James Parson,
                %em Moduli of elliptic curves
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.stanford.edu/~conrad/vigregroup/vigre03/moduli.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Mathew
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
                , section 3 of
                %em
                  The homotopy groups of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi TMF
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TMF
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~sglasman/tmfhomotopy.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Henriques"}> Andre Henriques
                ,
                %em The moduli stack of elliptic curves
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/2007/tmfproc/Chapter04/henriques.pdf"}> pdf
                ) in
                %em Topological modular forms
                Talbot workshop 2007 (
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/conferences/talbot/2007/tmfproc/"}> web
                )
          %p
            For more of the general picture in view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            see also
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+Euler+characteristic"} orbifold Euler characteristic
            of the moduli space of curves was originally computed in
          %ul
            %li#ZagierHarer86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Don+Zagier"}> Don Zagier
              , John Harer,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Euler characteristic of the moduli space of curves
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/143377"} EUDML
          %p Reviews of the orbifold Euler characteristic computation include
          %ul
            %li
              %em Mathematical ideas and notions in quantum field theory – 5. The Euler characteristic of the moduli space of curves
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/EulerCharacteristicOfSpaceOfCurves.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
